  "output": "## Reality check first\n\nThis isn't the failure mode the question assumes. The actual app (moved from repo root into `web/` earlier in this session — HANDOFF.md confirms it's a fresh wireframe drop) is pre-Phase-1 per AGENTS.md's own build order: no Drizzle client/schema (`web/lib/db/` is empty), no `engine/`, no API routes, no TanStack Query wiring. Grepping the whole `web/` tree turns up **zero** `useState`/`useEffect`/`useMemo`/`useCallback`, no subscriptions, no timers, no event listeners. Every route is a Server Component except 7 client-boundary leaves, and 6 of those exist solely to drive a `motion/react` entrance fade.\n\nSo: no unnecessary re-renders (nothing holds state to re-render on), no memory leaks (nothing subscribes to anything), no redundant client computations (nothing computes anything). Manufacturing findings there would be noise. There is exactly **one** real issue in the current code, and it matters more once `lib/db` exists.\n\n## The one real finding — duplicate full-table scan\n\n`web/lib/server/sources.ts`:\n\n```ts\nexport async function listSources(): Promise<Source[]> {\n  const rows = await db.select().from(sources).orderBy(sources.createdAt);\n  return rows.map((row) => sourceSchema.parse(row));\n}\n\nexport async function countSourcesBySide() {\n  const all = await listSources();          // full SELECT * + Zod-parse every row\n  return {\n    crm: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"salesforce\" || s.kind === \"hubspot\").length,\n    warehouse: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"databricks\" || s.kind === \"snowflake\").length,\n    synthetic: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"synthetic\").length,\n  };\n}\n```\n\n`app/get-started/page.tsx` only needs a count to decide button copy, but it pulls every row (including the `config` jsonb blob) and Zod-validates each one just to `.filter().length` it three times. `app/(console)/sources/page.tsx` does the same full scan again on a different request. This scales linearly with source count for no reason — a count doesn't need the rows.\n\n**Fix**, once `lib/db/client.ts` + `lib/db/schema.ts` land (currently missing — this and the query fix belong in the same commit):\n\n```ts\nimport { sql } from \"drizzle-orm\";\n\nexport async function countSourcesBySide() {\n  const rows = await db\n    .select({ kind: sources.kind, n: sql<number>`count(*)`.mapWith(Number) })\n    .from(sources)\n    .groupBy(sources.kind);\n\n  const byKind = Object.fromEntries(rows.map((r) => [r.kind, r.n]));\n  return {\n    crm: (byKind.salesforce ?? 0) + (byKind.hubspot ?? 0),\n    warehouse: (byKind.databricks ?? 0) + (byKind.snowflake ?? 0),\n    synthetic: byKind.synthetic ?? 0,\n  };\n}\n```\n\nIf both `/sources` and `/get-started` genuinely need to run in the same request tree later, wrap the read in React's `cache()` so Next.js dedupes it per-request instead of hitting Postgres twice:\n\n```ts\nimport { cache } from \"react\";\nexport const listSources = cache(async (): Promise<Source[]> => { ... });\n```\n\n## Forward-looking: where these bugs *will* show up (Phase 2–4)\n\nWorth flagging now since AGENTS.md's own architecture makes each of these near-certain, not hypothetical:\n\n**N+1 — the conflict queue.** `types/run.ts` and the schema imply `conflicts` joins to `matches` joins to `entities` (both sides) plus `resolutions`. A queue of \"400 conflicts\" (AGENTS.md's own number) built as one query per row will do 400+ round trips. Use Drizzle relational queries or a single joined `select` up front:\n```ts\nconst rows = await db.query.conflicts.findMany({\n  with: { match: { with: { entityA: true, entityB: true } }, resolution: true },\n  where: eq(conflicts.runId, runId),\n});\n```\n\n**Re-renders — the conflict queue's keyboard nav (`j`/`k`/`a`/`e`/`o`).** That's the one place this app will hold real client state. Keep the \"selected index\" in one small client component at the list boundary, not on each `ConflictDiffRow`; pass rows down as props from the Server Component parent so 400 rows don't each re-render on every keypress. Memoize `ConflictDiffRow` if row content is otherwise static.\n\n**Caching — run-status polling.** This is the one specified TanStack Query use case. Set `staleTime`/disable `refetchOnWindowFocus`, and stop polling on terminal status using the helper that already exists:\n```ts\nuseQuery({\n  queryKey: [\"run\", runId, \"status\"],\n  queryFn: () => fetchRunStatus(runId),\n  refetchInterval: (q) => (q.state.data && !isRunActive(q.state.data.status) ? false : 2000),\n});\n```\nAlso cache the ruleset block for prompt caching on the engine side (AGENTS.md already calls this out as the biggest cost lever) — don't rebuild that prompt segment per conflict.\n\n**Memory/blocking — the matching stage.** AGENTS.md is explicit: never all-pairs. When `pipeline/blocking.py` gets built, confirm FAISS top-k blocking is actually wired before any exact/fuzzy fallback runs O(n²), especially in `engine/eval/harness.py` sweeps over synthetic datasets sized in the hundreds of accounts.\n\n**Redundant computation — normalization.** `normalize()` folds name variants (case, punctuation, suffixes) — make sure that folding runs once per entity at ingest and gets stored (`normalizedName`), not recomputed per comparison inside the O(n·k) matching loop.\n\nNone of this needs action today — `lib/db` doesn't exist yet, so build it with the aggregate-query pattern above from the start rather than writing `listSources()`-style full scans first and fixing them later.\n",
